{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$\n- $N$\n- $Q$\n- ${Q}^{-}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042711/state.json" "file_sha256" "383f629ade178e8a4428aa6f36163125dd853dafe4480b32a24597f329a288de"} {"question" "q-36244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $N$ contains all the natural numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $N,$ so $N$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $Q$ contains all the rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $Q,$ so $Q$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042711/state.json" "file_sha256" "383f629ade178e8a4428aa6f36163125dd853dafe4480b32a24597f329a288de"} {"question" "q-36244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042711/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b157690bd8f9adc4402c9c4f827c40e98541b3f19f9164903547b5f01e0a5c83"} {"question" "q-36244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field